content.com/u/43268759?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/QuiiBz","html_url":"https://github.com/QuiiBz","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/QuiiBz/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/QuiiBz/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/QuiiBz/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/QuiiBz/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/QuiiBz/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/QuiiBz/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/QuiiBz/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/QuiiBz/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/QuiiBz/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2022-07-03T09:30:40Z","updated_at":"2022-07-03T10:22:00Z","body":"I searched a bit and the issue first appeared in version [12.1.1-canary.5](https://github.com/vercel/next.js/releases/tag/v12.1.1-canary.5).\r\n\r\nImporting `next/dist/cli/next-start` without calling `nextStart()` before this version does not start the server.\r\n\r\nedit:\r\nIt's a regression from https://github.com/vercel/next.js/pull/34836:\r\n\r\nWhen `getProjectDir` is called, it now also imports `next/bin/next.ts`, which is itself calling `commands[command]()`. \r\n\r\nThis `command` should not be defined, but it fallbacks to `defaultCommand`, which is `dev` (that explains why the dev server is also started)\r\n\r\n2nd edit:\r\nOpened a PR that fixes the issue: #38274 ","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vercel/next.js/issues/comments/1173046445/reactions","total_count":3,"+1":3,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"QuiiBz","id":43268759,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQzMjY4NzU5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/43268759?v=4","gravatar